+#!/usr/bin/env python
+# Copyright (c) 2026, HUAWEI CORPORATION.  All rights reserved.
+#
+# Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
+"""Self-tests for the Qwen3.8-Flash-Next PLE port (``qwen4_exp``).
+
+Sections, each runnable on its own with ``--stage``:
+
+1. ``import``  -- the module imports and the two classes expose the interface the
+   layer and the bridge call them through;
+2. ``tensors`` -- the three int64 index buffers *derived from the config* equal
+   the ones the checkpoint stores, for the release's own geometry (needs the
+   checkpoint; constructing the module also allocates this rank's rows of the
+   table, and ``--with-table`` fills them out of the real 128-shard table and
+   reads a few rows back, which is the only way to check the shard indexing
+   against the files it will actually run on);
+3. ``hash``    -- ``ngram_ids`` equals a naive transcription of the reference's
+   own loop, including the EOS reset and the sample boundaries of a packed
+   stream, plus the boundaries themselves and the two arrays they are read from;
+4. ``table``   -- ``PinnedNGramTable`` hands back exactly the rows a dense
+   ``index`` of the whole matrix would, reading a sharded safetensors table
+   through mmap or from the tensors a load hands over, with and without the
+   checkpoint's index file, and refuses the tables it cannot read (missing shard,
+   unaligned shard, ragged split). It is also where the tensor-parallel row shard
+   is checked: a rank materializes its own rows and zeros for everyone else's,
+   which is the sum the lookup finishes on the device;
+5. ``layer``   -- the whole ``Qwen4ExpTextPLELayer`` chain equals an inline
+   transcription of HF's ``Qwen4ExpTextPLELayer.forward`` (grouped norms, gate,
+   dilated depthwise conv) on a packed batch, which the reference runs one row
+   per sample, plus the receptive field those two windows imply and the fact
+   that neither window reaches across a sample boundary or a sample's padding;
+6. ``layout``  -- the sequence-parallel path: ``_keep_own_chunk`` takes the
+   rank's own chunk and its backward zero-fills every other one (which is what
+   keeps the parameter gradients out of the sequence-parallel sum's way), and a
+   two-rank world emulated by hand round-trips through ``forward`` -- in the
+   sharded layout too, where the lookup hands back this rank's rows of the whole
+   stream's partial and the conv takes the frames before this chunk off the rank
+   before it;
+7. ``conv``    -- the sharded convolution against the full-sequence one, bit for
+   bit, over split packed streams that put a sample boundary at, before and
+   inside the first frames of a chunk (no NPU, no group);
+8. ``export``  -- the table's shard-at-a-time export: every row of a shard, in
+   the checkpoint's own order, assembled in pieces;
+9. ``trainable`` -- the table as a device *parameter* instead of a host buffer
+   (``QWEN4_EXP_PLE_CPU_OFFLOAD=0``): that it is built as one, that a module
+   transform carries it, that it is left out of the sequence-parallel sweep, that
+   it takes the loaded shards, and that it shares the buffer form's state dict;
+   the routed lookup and its gradient run on a real EP group in stage 11;
+10. ``sp2``     -- the sharded layout against the full-sequence one on **two dies**,
+   under a real tensor-parallel group, so the three collectives the six stages
+   above emulate (the gather, the reduce-scatter, the differentiable halo
+   all-gather) run for real and the two layouts still have to agree;
+11. ``ep``      -- the expert-parallel table: first the two-way form switch
+   (``QWEN4_EXP_PLE_TABLE_MODE``) against the older offload switch, then, on **two
+   dies**, the row-routed lookup over a real EP group -- the owner map, the count
+   exchange that yields both split vectors, the variable-split request and return
+   exchanges, and the return exchange's mirrored backward -- checked numerically
+   against a dense table and structurally by where a row's gradient lands. Both
+   forward layouts run: the sequence-parallel one, which routes only this rank's
+   chunk, and the whole-sequence one, which splits the lookup over the group and
+   gathers it back so the gradient is not multiplied by the number of ranks.
+
+Stages 2-4 and 7 run without an NPU. Stages 5-6 and 9 build the layer, which
+allocates on the device (``ReplicatedLinear`` asks for it), and compare on the
+host, so they need an NPU and a one-rank process group. Stages 10 and 11 spawn
+two children of this file, one per die, so they need two free dies
+(``QWEN4_EXP_PLE_SP2_DEVICES`` / ``QWEN4_EXP_PLE_EP_DEVICES``, default ``0,1``)
+and take them for as long as the stage runs. Stage 11's first half needs no die
+at all, so ``--stage ep`` on an otherwise busy box still checks the switch.
+
+The context-parallel split/gather pair is *not* tested here: it is
+``cp_split.cp_local_index`` against ``qsa.cp_utils.reconstruct_tensor_cp``, both
+already exercised by the QSA work, and the CP runs cover them end to end. What
+this file pins is what would otherwise first fail inside a 125B training step.
+
+Usage::
+
+    python mindspeed_bridge/models/qwen4_exp/modelling_qwen4_exp/tests/test_ple.py
+    python .../tests/test_ple.py --stage hash
+    python .../tests/test_ple.py --stage tensors --checkpoint "${QWEN4_EXP_CKPT}" --with-table
+
+By path, not ``-m``: ``-m`` imports the ``qwen4_exp`` package first, and that package
+imports the bridge, which imports ``megatron.bridge`` and so ``transformer_engine_torch``
+-- a module that does not exist until the adaptor has installed its stand-in. The file
+imports the plugin lazily, after its own :func:`_setup_npu`, so the bootstrap is not
+needed here (``align_with_hf``, which does not control its own imports, respawns itself
+instead).
+
+It never trains and never builds a model.
+"""
+
