+"""Model provider for Qwen3.8-Flash-Next (``qwen4_exp``).
+
+The provider is the Megatron configuration of the checkpoint: every field the
+layer modules read (``config.hc_count``, ``config.indexer_*``, ...) is declared
+here with the value of the released model, so that a provider built from the HF
+config and a provider built from defaults describe the same network.
+
+Architecture (the text tower; the released checkpoint also carries a vision
+tower, see the VL bridge):
+
+* 48 layers, groups of ``3 x linear_attention + 1 x full_attention``;
+* hidden size 2560, 24 query heads of 256 channels, 2 KV heads;
+* ``hc_count=4`` gated hyper-connection streams, mixed through rank-320
+  low-rank mixers (``hc_lowrank``);
+* every layer is MoE: 512 routed experts (top-10, intermediate 640) plus a
+  shared expert of 640 with its own gate;
+* one MTP head, which re-reads the *un-contracted* hyper-connection streams;
+* mRoPE with interleaved ``[11, 11, 10]`` sections over a quarter of the head
+  channels, ``rope_theta=1e7``;
+* no per-layer layernorms at all, and zero-centered RMSNorm gammas -- except
+  for the GDN output norm, which ``provide()`` opts out (see
+  :func:`~mindspeed_bridge.models.qwen4_exp.modelling_qwen4_exp.gdn.fix_gdn_out_norm_zero_centered`).
+"""
